"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. A call for ideas regarding AI-enhanced data visualization was issued with a July 20th deadline. The project celebrated the completion of the testing phase on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November. Recent updates include finalizing technical documentation, scheduling a steering committee meeting, and preparing for a showcase event. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, were updated to take effect in January. Additionally, a $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
